Z||000002||StuGood||10-19-2000||01:06 PM||||All other things being equal, 4-speed will probably get better gas mileage.  Since you're comparing two auto-trans cars at this point, it's kind of acedemic.<P>FWIW, my 1986 SE 4-speed got about 28-ish mpg highway when new.  My 1987 5-speed GT gets 29-32 mpg highway.  I own a V6 automatic, but no mileage data.  As the ads say, "Your actual mileage may vary."  In fact, your mileage <B>will</B> vary.<P>If you're interested in a reliable highway car, I'd tend to go with the lower odometer reading, or the one that looks better taken care of, in general.  The GT is heavier and might make a better highway cruiser - more because GT's tend to come loaded with more optional equipment.<P>Since the GT is heavier, expect to pay a slight penalty for gas and speed.  So get the  1986 SE, and save the GT for Stu  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !      <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||10-19-2000||10:30 PM||||i have a 86gt i travel 25 miles from home to work and back,now i fill the tank up on sunday and i will not fill up again till next sunday,now i also use the car for errands or for a drive and i still fill up till next sunday plus i have the power to move me,if i was you i would buy the gt and paint it,gas mileage is achieved if you sevice the car right and drive it normal you will get good gas mileage out of it,so the choise is yours,good luck.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
